# Build-time configuration for production builds.
#
# THIS FILE IS COMMITTED ON PURPOSE, and it is safe to commit.
#
# Every value here is a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable, which means Next.js inlines it
# into the JavaScript bundle that ships to every visitor's browser. They are
# public by definition — anyone can read them with View Source. Keeping them
# in the repo leaks nothing that the built site does not already publish.
#
# Why not Netlify's dashboard variables? Because a build that depends on
# dashboard state fails silently: the site builds, deploys and looks correct,
# while the booking widget and contact form quietly do nothing. That exact
# failure already happened once here. Committing them makes any build, on any
# machine or CI provider, produce a working site with no configuration step.
#
# Real secrets never go here. The Turnstile SECRET key and the n8n API key are
# not in this repo at all — the Turnstile secret lives only in the n8n
# "Verify Turnstile" node, and the n8n key only in ~/.zshenv.
#
# Netlify dashboard variables still win if set, since process.env takes
# precedence over .env files. This is the fallback, not an override.

NEXT_PUBLIC_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://jcmt.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/fasteradmin-contact
NEXT_PUBLIC_AVAILABILITY_ENDPOINT=https://jcmt.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/fasteradmin-availability
NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_ENDPOINT=https://jcmt.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/fasteradmin-book

# Legacy shared token, checked by the n8n abuse gate. Also public by design.
# Turnstile is the real protection; drop this once the gate stops checking it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FA_TOKEN=KeB_w7j2FRkIvV5CmTxJMpZl1PEAV3Yw

# Cloudflare Turnstile SITE key. Public half of the pair.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAAEG7UrQD4GCu6M7E
